WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.618
Now we deliberately violate the scalar contract The
inner query

00:00:05.644 --> 00:00:11.195
returns many patient IDs from admissions The outer
expression

00:00:11.222 --> 00:00:17.038
expects one value PostgreSQL cannot choose one row
for you so

00:00:17.051 --> 00:00:22.656
it raises an error Do not automatically add LIMIT
one just to remove

00:00:22.682 --> 00:00:28.356
the error Only do that if choosing an arbitrary
single row actually matches the business

00:00:28.382 --> 00:00:28.763
meaning
